---
// Goal: take a reader from Liquid's console to a key, a passing check, and a first answer from d1.
import SidePage from '../../../layouts/SidePage.astro';
import Terminal from '../../../components/Terminal.astro';
import BackendFacts from '../../../components/BackendFacts.astro';
import { BACKEND_PAGES, BACKENDS_SEE, KEY_VARIABLE } from '../../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { captioned } from '../../../data/samples.mjs';
import { backend } from '../../../lib/backends-table.mjs';
import { checkLines } from '../../../data/backend-checks.mjs';
import { setting } from '../../../lib/settings-table.mjs';

const page = BACKEND_PAGES.find((p) => p.slug === 'liquid');
const b = backend('liquid');
const runs = captioned('install/backends/liquid', BACKENDS_SEE.liquid);
const by = (name) => runs.find((r) => r.name.endsWith(name));
const [status, one, lines, plan] = ['status', 'one', 'lines', 'check-plan'].map(by);
const checks = checkLines('liquid');
const timeout = setting('Timeout').default;
---
<SidePage pages={BACKEND_PAGES} page={{ ...page, description: "Liquid's d1 decision model through ThinkThen: the key from Liquid's console, the address, the model, the check, and a first answer." }} name="Backends">
  <h1>Liquid d1</h1>
  <p class="lede">d1 is Liquid's decision model. Its server speaks System One, so ThinkThen asks it with no change but the backend name.</p>

  <BackendFacts name="liquid" />
  <p>Liquid launched d1 on 2026-09-29. Its models endpoint gives a release date of 2026-09-22. On 2026-09-30 that endpoint listed one model, <code>{b.model}</code>, and Liquid published no price for it. Its replies count input tokens only, and output tokens are always zero.</p>

  <h2>Get a key</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Sign in at <a href="https://console.liquid.ai">console.liquid.ai</a>.</li>
    <li>Open Dashboard, then API Keys, and create a key. It starts with <code>liquid_</code>.</li>
    <li>Put it in <code>{b.keys[0]}</code>. ThinkThen also reads <code>{b.keys[1]}</code> when the first is unset.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>These steps were checked on 2026-09-29.</p>
  <Terminal run={status} caption={status.see} />

  <h2>Check it</h2>
  <p>A first check can take longer than the default timeout of {timeout}. Pass <code>--timeout 90</code> on the first run.</p>
  <Terminal run={plan} caption={plan.see} />
  {checks.map((c) => <p>{c.said} <a href={c.record}>The record</a> holds the report.</p>)}

  {one && lines ? (
    <Fragment>
      <h2>A first answer</h2>
      <Terminal run={one} caption={one.see} />
      <Terminal run={lines} caption={lines.see} />
    </Fragment>
  ) : (
    <p>This page shows no recorded d1 answer. The <a href="/install/backends/typesafe/">TypeSafe Jev page</a> asks the same two questions.</p>
  )}

  <h2>Without the backend name</h2>
  <p>The address and a key work without the name too. Set <code>THINKTHEN_BASE_URL={b.base}</code>, put the key in <code>{KEY_VARIABLE}</code>, and pass <code>--model {b.model}</code>.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/install/backends/">All backends</a> · <a href="/install/configuration/">Configuration</a></p>
</SidePage>
